 bug_trends.py, docs, tests — but no scripts/ entry."],"finding":"The plan enumerates the caused_by write sites that should set the new provenance marker — `_apply_caused_by` (transition_close) and `add_dependency` (rebar link) — but omits `scripts/backfill_caused_by.py`, which writes caused_by edges via `_write_link_event` from blame auto-derivation (`derive_caused_by`). That is a blame-derived write path directly analogous to the `_apply_caused_by` derived case, yet neither the write-site list nor the Scope file list mentions it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f221db076dc46ab43","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach / Scope — the caused_by write-site inventory (`_apply_caused_by` passes derived/explicit; `add_dependency` marks explicit)","norm_id":"ndad42309d1c8d534","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["scripts/backfill_caused_by.py's backfill() draws retroactive caused_by edges over closed bugs from blame; if not included in the marker rollout it writes these edges with no provenance, so they read as 'unknown' instead of 'derived' and the bug_caused_by_provenance dimension miscounts backfilled guesses — defeating the derived/explicit partition the ticket exists to enable."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"In backfill()'s write loop, pass `provenance=\"derived\"` to `_write_link_event` (the culprit comes from `derive_caused_by`), and list scripts/backfill_caused_by.py in Scope with a regression test that a backfilled edge reduces to `provenance == \"derived\"`.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no